<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-four-types" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>The Four Exercise Types in PreTeXt</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Each section of this chapter implements one of the course's four
      exercise types in several ways, all using the <c>find_min</c> material
      from block 8 of the syllabus. The last section does the same with Sage
      cells only, for comparison. The analysis
      behind it (<q>The four exercise types in a PreTeXt interactive
      book</q>) is part of the course's syllabus documents.
      <xref ref="ch-block06"/> uses the recommended techniques for a whole
      block.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="types-predict.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="types-gapfill.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="types-fixbug.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="types-write.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="types-sage.ptx" />
</chapter>
